<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:1.7pt;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:1.7pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt'><span style='mso-bookmark:OLE_LINK2'><span
style='font-size:9.0pt'><span style='mso-tab-count:1'>               </span>The
Joint Pipeline Office is a consortium of six State and six Federal agencies
with oversight responsibilities for the Trans-Alaska Pipeline System and other
oil and gas pipelines in </span></span><st1:State><st1:place><span
  style='mso-bookmark:OLE_LINK2'><span style='font-size:9.0pt'>Alaska</span></span></st1:place></st1:State><span
style='mso-bookmark:OLE_LINK2'><span style='font-size:9.0pt'>.<span
style='mso-spacerun:yes'>  </span>The JPO came into existence in 1990 and
stemmed from a cooperative effort by the Bureau of Land Management and the
Alaska Department of Natural Resources.</span></span><span style='font-size:
9.0pt'><o:p></o:p></span></p>

